session Relative_Arbitrage = Covariation_Constrained_Martingales +
  description "
    Theorem 1.1 of Lai, Shkolnikov and Soner, Relative arbitrage problem under
    eigenvalue lower bounds (arXiv:2512.17702): the value function of the
    minimum-exit-time problem under eigenvalue constraints on the covariation
    is the unique bounded upper semicontinuous viscosity solution of the
    associated degenerate elliptic equation.

    The operator of Eq. (1.9), its envelopes, the subspace-tangential field
    and the comparison principle (Theorem 4.2(a)) are in the probability-free
    session Relative_Arbitrage_Equation (the comparison chain itself, for
    any geometric operator, in Geometric_Viscosity_Comparison); the
    operations on path laws (cutting, glueing, shifting, sampling at a
    stopping time) and the class of laws
    with constrained covariation are in Path_Space_Operations, and its
    compactness, pasting and dynamic programming principle, for an arbitrary
    constraint set, are in Covariation_Constrained_Martingales.  This session
    instantiates that class at the eigenvalue constraint set of Eq. (1.7)
    and proves the five clauses for its value function: the viscosity
    verification and uniqueness for an abstract constraint set, then their
    instances.
  "
  options [document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    Relative_Arbitrage_Equation
  theories
    Control_Problem
    Proposition_2_4
    Value_Function_Subsolution
    Euler_Limit_Growth
    Value_Function_Tangential_Field
    Value_Function_Supersolution
    Example_3_1
    Covariation_Operator
    Value_Function_Uniqueness
    Exit_Class_Infinite
    Exit_Class_Marginals
    Exit_Class_Expected_Exit_Time
    Theorem_1_1
